<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Why Best Hydrate exists">
  <div><strong>Start with the problem</strong><span>Hydration advice can be fragmented, overmarketed or disconnected from how people actually drink during a real day.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Use the mechanism</strong><span>Glucose, sodium and water transport provide a physiological foundation for explaining oral hydration without pretending one formula fits every context.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Keep improving</strong><span>Product development, research and public education are treated as an ongoing system rather than a finished marketing claim.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">The origin</p>
    <h2>It began with a personal need for hydration that felt more deliberate</h2>
    <p>After a serious health experience, founder Austin began looking more closely at what hydration products contained, how oral fluid absorption works and why so many products were positioned primarily around flavour, sugar avoidance or generic electrolyte language.</p>
    <p>The company grew from that curiosity. The aim became broader than making another flavoured powder: build a hydration product around understandable physiology, make the ingredient logic visible, and create a platform that can support performance, everyday, clinical-development and humanitarian questions without pretending those use cases are identical.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Core idea</span>
    <h3>Hydration is a system, not a slogan.</h3>
    <p>Water access, electrolytes, carbohydrate, environment, health status and behaviour can all matter. The right emphasis changes with context.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__split">
  <div class="bhd-page__split-media">
    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/8392542/pexels-photo-8392542.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Scientist using a dropper during a laboratory procedure" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
